dzil build aborts before it produces a tarball:

    [@Author::GETTY/LicenseFile] no LICENSE in the distribution:
    run 'dzil genlicense' and commit the file

There is no LICENSE file in the repository. dist.ini declares `license = Perl_5` and `copyright_holder = Torsten Raudssus`, so genlicense has everything it needs.

Pre-existing, not introduced by any of the current work - found while verifying the karr #5 fix. It is a hard release blocker: no build, no tarball, and the release-checker cannot do its job either.

Fix: run `dzil genlicense`, check the generated text names the right holder and year, and commit the file.
Fixed and committed. dzil genlicense produced LICENSE (Perl_5, 2026 Torsten Raudssus) and it is now tracked - the tracking is the load-bearing half, since Git::GatherDir ships tracked files only. dzil build now runs through and writes Crypt-Age-0.002.tar.gz. No release attempted.
